# Test: MonadMaybe.bind — bind a Some value through a transformation.
# MonadMaybe is defined in prelude.llt as an instance of the Monad typeclass.
# The type checker does not know about MonadMaybe (no prelude type env seeding),
# so it warns "undefined variable: MonadMaybe", but the evaluator succeeds.
[MonadMaybe.bind [Some 42] [fn [let x] [Some [+ x 1]]]]
=== out
Variant(Maybe.Some, Int(43))

=== warn
[NotARecord] expected record type, got <error>
